From 1daa762ded4ba2313da15f685208c3b168690f2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Gonzalez <dev@gonzalezerik.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:05:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 03/15] bsps/powerpc/ibookg3: Add PCI and ATA support

Read the UniNorth host bridge base and the /pci interrupt-map from the
device tree and implement the shared powerpc PCI configuration space
interface through the bridge's memory-mapped address and data windows,
with the slow-latching address register verified by readback. Each
device's interrupt line register is seeded with its OpenPIC source so
drivers only need PCI_INTERRUPT_LINE, matching the powermac firmware.

Add a KeyLargo ATA backend for the shared RTEMS IDE/ATA layer. The
taskfile registers sit 0x10 bytes apart with the device control
register at 0x160; only the data register is touched as words, which
also settles the byte order: plain big endian word accesses through the
guarded window leave the IDENTIFY data in the layout the ATA layer's
little endian word parsing expects, verified against the drive model
string. Transfers stay in the firmware's PIO mode; the KeyLargo DMA
timings are not programmed.

The Open Firmware probe additionally collects the two ata-3 children of
the mac-io node (bus id, reg offset, interrupt source) and the UniNorth
base; defaults apply when the device tree is not available.
